---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import LegalIdentity from '../../components/LegalIdentity.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, LAST_UPDATED, LEGAL, SITE_NAMES, SITE_URL } from '../../data/site-config';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
const lang = 'en';
---
<PageLayout title={`Privacy policy of ${SITE_NAMES[lang]}: no inputs leave your browser`} description="What personal data this stamp duty calculator processes (almost none), on what legal basis, for how long, and how to use your rights or complain to the ICO or the CNIL." lang={lang} noindex={true} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Privacy' }]} showAuthor={false}>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none prose-headings:font-serif">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p>This policy covers {SITE_URL}. The publisher is established in France, so the EU General Data Protection Regulation applies; for visitors in the United Kingdom, the UK GDPR and the Data Protection Act 2018 give the same rights.</p>
    <h2>1. Controller</h2>
    <LegalIdentity lang={lang} />
    <h2>2. What the calculator never sends</h2>
    <p>Prices, nations, buyer situations and dates are processed in your browser only. They are not sent to a server, not stored and not linked to you. The share link writes your inputs into the page address: only send it to people you choose.</p>
    <h2>3. What is processed</h2>
    <h3>Server logs</h3><p>The host records the IP address, time, page requested and browser, for security. Legal basis: legitimate interest. Retention: according to GitHub’s policy.</p>
    <h3>Audience measurement</h3><p>None is loaded today. If one is added, you will be told by a banner before it runs and you will be able to refuse it, and this page will list it.</p>
    <h3>E-mails</h3><p>If you write to us, your address and message are kept to answer you, for three years after the last exchange.</p>
    <h2>4. Recipients and transfers</h2><p>Nothing is sold or shared. The host, GitHub, Inc., is in the United States; logs may be processed there under the EU–US Data Privacy Framework and its UK extension.</p>
    <h2>5. Your rights</h2><p>Access, correction, erasure, restriction, objection and portability: write to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>; we reply within one month. You can complain to the {LEGAL.supervisoryAuthority} (<a href={LEGAL.supervisoryAuthorityUrl} rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">{LEGAL.supervisoryAuthorityUrl}</a>) or, in the UK, to the Information Commissioner’s Office (<a href="https://ico.org.uk" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">ico.org.uk</a>).</p>
    <h2>6. No automated decision</h2><p>A result is an estimate you ask for; it has no legal effect on you.</p>
    <p>See also the <a href={route('cookies', lang)}>cookies page</a>. Updated: {LAST_UPDATED}.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
